Exercise
 R (A, B, C, D)
 S = {A→B, B→C, C→D, D→A} 
 What are all the keys of R?
 What are all the super-keys for R that are not keys?
 Answer:
 {A}+={ABCD}
 {B}+={ABCD}
 {C}+={ABCD}
 {D}+={ABCD}
 → Keys: {A}, {B}, {C}, {D}
 → Super-keys: add any attribute to the keys.

